There is not way of guaranteedly "hacking" someone's account without them giving you permission or if it's not protected properly with strong security settings, but there are many steps you can take to increase your chances of being able to access the account if you are the person they have authorized. First and foremost, do not ever share account credentials (logins/password) with anyone else; your username, name, email and a phone number must all match theirs. Then log onto your account from your phone number via security code SMS; this protects it if someone is looking to steal credentials off your phone number. Secondly, only share apps you need with access with your facebook account with them directly from the phone number it is linked to. Thirdly, enabling multi-factor authentication; this includes verifying your identity with items such as a code sent to your email, code from their messenger and security key fob will secure your account even if credentials are stolen. In general; secure it! (last tip).
(Source: Facebook’s guide to ‘Securing’ your account [Facebook]) #FacebookSecurity #FacebookPrivacy #Hacking
